  :doc/body
  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 31

This is the quiet rematch of `kernel_deep` versus LLVM.
Iteration 07 said 1.44x after proportional spilling (from 7.87x).
That ranking was never rematched on quiet judah through the
hoisted runner. This file is that rematch. Encodings are not a ranking.

Do not overwrite 04-30. Do not rematch `kernel_wide` (iteration 14).
Do not ship rust sources into amu.

## What was timed

Compiled from an amu worktree at pin `27d69898aca60db492d2c415eae31d7a72a07243`
(not the stale shared checkout). `deps.edn` at that pin names
kotoba-native `4bb08b9228bc41168ab42bf6d7d2e60150104aff` and
kotoba-mir `767d3c0b418f85d1d177f78b0648c106a79bfb62`.

| arm | what ran | bytes / offset | sha256 |
|---|---|---:|---|
| amu | `kernel_deep.kotoba` → extract-native `--symbol kernel` | **1068 B / 0** | `18c0f6a78bc8b7e6cd6b18e9e6a32f8d7a94839b0fecf1da8f0c558051052976` |
| llvm | `rustc --edition 2021 -C opt-level=3 -C codegen-units=1 kernel_deep.rs` | Mach-O | `2d1481181378677951e0033d8bc3abfbd9faf2fc242715d08d9c47eb9f2f0b4a` |

amu first word `f353bfa9` (STP). 24 SMULH + 2 MUL in the extracted body.
The 24-lane leaf is still a leaf. LLVM did not delete the work.

LLVM was compiled on this Air (`rustc 1.97.1 (8bab26f4f 2026-07-14)`,
aarch64-apple-darwin) because judah has no rustc. Timing ran on **judah**.
This Air is not a ranking host (loadavg ~25 during the compile).

Runner: judah `/tmp/kexe-benchmark-iter29` (isa hoisted; reused, not rebuilt).
n=200, 100k calls, 10k warmup — same leaf-fixture protocol as iteration 14.

## Oracle

Harness `warmup=0` and `n=0` are outside the admitted range. One-shot used
1 call and 1 warmup. Result **2552249090** on both arms, no trap. The same
result held on every scored sample. STOP was not taken.

## Times

12 discarded frequency-warmup rotations (two arms rotated), then 25
scored rotated samples. Judge: **min ns/call** reported; **perfgate
uses means**.

judah loadavg `{ 1.88 1.59 1.57 }` start and end. load1 stayed under 4.

| arm | min | mean | median | p95 | max | rel stdev |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| amu | 9.77 | 9.9528 | 9.94 | 10.22 | 10.22 | 0.0107 |
| llvm | 8.928 | 9.230 | 9.239 | 9.506 | 9.547 | 0.0189 |

min ratio amu/llvm **1.094x**. mean ratio **1.078x**.
mean improvement **-7.83%**.

Dump: `/tmp/iter31-dump/` (`kernel_deep.bin`, `kernel_deep.kexe`,
`kernel_deep-llvm`, `kernel_deep-llvm.s`, `samples.json`, `arms.edn`,
`qualify.clj`, `qualify.edn`).

## perfgate

`perfgate.core/qualify` on the 25 ns/call vectors. Candidate = amu,
baseline = llvm, metric `:wall-ns`, unit `\"ns/call\"`. Machine
descriptor `:measured` from `ssh judah sysctl hw.ncpu hw.pagesize
hw.cachelinesize hw.l1dcachesize hw.l2cachesize machdep.cpu.brand_string`
(ncpu 10, pagesize 16384, cachelinesize 128, l1d 65536, l2 4194304,
brand Apple M4). ways not reported; not fabricated. perfgate
`d4417d77`, machine `4f57144a`.

- mean improvement **-7.83%** (required +5%)
- gap **0.723 ns** > summed stdev **0.281 ns** (separated)
- relative stdev 0.0107 / 0.0189 (allowed 0.10)
- `:improvement-below-threshold`
- `:qualified? false`
- **no claim artifact**

The arms are apart. LLVM is faster. The gap is smaller than the gate
anyway. Do not claim amu beats LLVM. Do not write 1.09x into
`amu/docs/performance.md` as a pin-moving result. The 1.44x in
iteration 07 stays in that file; this file supersedes it as the
quiet-host ranking, not as a deletion.

`:llvm-beaten` remains false. The wide-leaf ranking (iteration 14)
stays refused. Do not rematch `kernel_wide`.

## Pins

No pin bump. The ranking used the pins iteration 28 already landed:

- kotoba-mir `767d3c0b418f85d1d177f78b0648c106a79bfb62`
- kotoba-native `4bb08b9228bc41168ab42bf6d7d2e60150104aff`
- amu `27d69898aca60db492d2c415eae31d7a72a07243`
- perfgate `d4417d77c2333047dd4e478675e5ed13e1c6b1b8`
- machine `4f57144aa6d3c240eb23c44dacab0b7ad5f5c505`

## What this does not change

- Timed `bench` export stays refused (iteration 4 / 5).
- `:llvm-beaten` remains false. Wide-leaf refusal (14) stands.
- `:cfg-liveness` remains false. last-uses are still textual.
- Production `:call-live` vs all-vreg (29) stays sealed.
- rustc arms stay in `/tmp/iter31-dump/`. They are not amu sources.
- west pins were not moved.
- `back-edge?` was not restored as a production short-circuit.

